WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.220
Which EU sovereignty
yardstick applies to us?

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.130
A framework we can use today,
or a law that may bind tomorrow.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.000
First, two yardsticks.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.990
The Commission's Cloud Sovereignty
Framework is a procurement tool.

00:00:14.255 --> 00:00:15.725
It has five SEAL levels.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.230
The Cloud and AI Development
Act is a proposal.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.420
It has four assurance levels.

00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:24.295
They would bind every
public buyer in the EU.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.920
So one is guidance today,
and the other is not yet law.

00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:30.713
Second, how the levels work.

00:00:31.023 --> 00:00:35.053
In the framework, the lowest of
eight objectives sets the SEAL level.

00:00:35.298 --> 00:00:38.228
Under the proposal,
level 1 is self-assessed.

00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:41.548
Levels 2 to 4 need an independent audit.

00:00:41.913 --> 00:00:44.683
A national authority
recognises the result,

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.103
and the service is listed
in an EU repository.

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:51.167
Third, who would have to comply.

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:55.257
Public bodies would decide which
activities count as public order,

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.557
and use level 2, 3 or 4 for those.

00:00:58.927 --> 00:01:01.337
Everything else needs level 1 at least.

00:01:01.702 --> 00:01:03.512
Private companies are not bound.

00:01:03.947 --> 00:01:05.477
Providers choose recognition,

00:01:06.087 --> 00:01:08.457
but without it there
is no public contract.

00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:11.947
Fourth, the level follows the activity.

00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:13.437
For municipalities,

00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.307
HR and finance would need level 1.

00:01:16.562 --> 00:01:17.312
For hospitals,

00:01:17.682 --> 00:01:20.092
patient care could need level 2 or 3.

00:01:20.347 --> 00:01:22.997
For courts, case files would need level 3.

00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:26.922
If a service sits at the wrong level,
the clock would be twelve months.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.260
What good looks like.

00:01:29.545 --> 00:01:32.515
An activity map,
with a level for each activity.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.960
Suppliers scored on both ladders.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.320
Level 2 clauses in contracts.

00:01:37.795 --> 00:01:40.245
And a tested exit for critical services.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:43.440
A suggested first step.

00:01:43.725 --> 00:01:45.055
Decide three things.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.890
Which activities would
count as public order.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.830
Which level we want from
each critical supplier.

00:01:51.155 --> 00:01:54.825
And whether to run the voluntary
assessment before anyone asks.

00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:57.973
One ladder to use today.

00:01:58.243 --> 00:01:59.673
One proposal to watch.

